    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="3120c855-5b1c-540c-ae9e-84d0380661be" activityNameId="26e6c9cd-e73d-552b-8e19-f48d80aae5b0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Nuclear power plant, pressure water reactor 1000MW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Nuclear power plant, pressure water reactor 1000MW
The module is based on "nuclear power plant, pressure water reactor 1000MW", CH. Only difference is the supply mix of electricity, DE instead of CH.;
UUID: 72cbd627-f72a-3a82-8e06-c4dec3f61cfd
The module includes materials, energy and transport requirements used for construction of the plant. Land-use is included with the assumption of 40 years operation. Disposal of non-contaminated material from dismantling is also included, whereas contaminated materials are attributed to the operation.
Location: Extrapolated from Swiss data on one specific plant.
Technology: The described plant Gösgen started commercial operation at the end of 1979. It belongs to the 1000 MW class. It has a Siemens designed primary circuit with three loop cooling, a spherical containment, and a cooling tower. This module can be assumed to be representative for German pressure water reactors of the same class.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_72cbd627-f72a-3a82-8e06-c4dec3f61cfd.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
